<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-8899] IgniteJdbcDriver directly create JavaLogger in static context</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-8899</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It means, that it always prints error in logs, if Jul logging file doesn&apos;t exist. I suggest to use the same approach as in thin driver:&lt;br/&gt;
replace &lt;br/&gt;
new JavaLogger()&lt;br/&gt;
with&lt;br/&gt;
Logger.getLogger(IgniteJdbcDriver.class.getName())&lt;/p&gt;</description>
